---
title: New York-Style Bagels
tags:
  - bread
  - breakfast
  - yeasted dough
servings: 12
---

-- ===== DOUGH =====

Combine @warm water{530%g} (86°F/30°C) and @instant yeast{1%tsp} -- approx. 3g -- in a medium bowl and stir to dissolve the yeast.

Add @bread flour{940%g}, @diastatic malt powder{1%tbsp} -- approx. 10g, or substitute 10g sugar -- and @salt{20%g} to the bowl, then mix with a sturdy spoon until a shaggy dough forms and you can no longer stir with the spoon.

Switch to a soaking wet hand and continue mixing the dough by squeezing and folding until well combined.

-- Optional: rest the dough at this point instead of kneading straight away.
Autolyse the dough by covering and resting it for ~{15%minutes} -- this lets the flour hydrate and gluten begin forming passively, reducing the kneading time needed below.

Transfer the dough to a work surface and knead for ~{10-12%minutes} until smooth and elastic -- when adequately kneaded, you should be able to tug on a piece of dough without it tearing.

-- ===== BULK FERMENT & SHAPE =====

Place the kneaded dough into a #bowl{}, cover with a lid, and let it bulk ferment at room temperature for ~{1%hour} -- it should rise by about 50%.

Cut the dough into 12 pieces, each weighing approximately 120g.

Shape each piece by pressing it out into a rectangle, then, starting with the edge furthest from you, roll the dough onto itself, pressing into the work surface with each roll until you have a cigar shape -- continue rolling until it's roughly 25cm long.

Wrap the dough log around your fingers, overlapping by about 8cm, and squeeze firmly to seal each end together.

With the dough still wrapped around your hand, roll it back and forth on the seam side to fully integrate and shape it into a bagel.

Place the shaped bagels onto two parchment-lined #sheet tray{2} lightly sprayed with pan spray, then cover with plastic wrap or half sheet tray covers.

Move the trays to the refrigerator and cold ferment for at least ~{4%hours}, preferably ~{24%hours}.

-- ===== BOIL & BAKE =====

Preheat your #oven{} to 245°C (475°F) and soak @bagel boards{} -- cedar planks with burlap stapled to them -- in water.

Bring @water{3-4%l} to a boil in a large #pot{} and add @black treacle{50%g}.

Cut the parchment around each bagel to make handling easier.

Carefully drop 3 bagels into the boiling water, top side down, and boil for ~{30%seconds}, then flip and boil for another ~{30%seconds} on the other side.

Transfer the boiled bagels to a #baking sheet{}, bottom side down, then repeat in batches of 3 for the remaining bagels.

Place the boiled bagels onto the soaked bagel boards, top side down, and bake for ~{5%minutes} -- I like to place mine directly on a pizza stone or steel.

Flip the bagels so the top side is up and continue baking for ~{12-15%minutes} until golden brown and blistered.

Remove the bagels from the oven and transfer to a #wire rack{} to cool.

-- ===== SEEDED VARIATION =====

-- After boiling, immediately press bagels into a tray of your chosen seeds (e.g. everything bagel seasoning, poppy seeds) top side down, then place on soaked bagel boards seed side down and bake as above.

-- ===== EVERYTHING BAGEL SEASONING =====

-- Equal parts by weight -- weight gives more consistent results than volume for a mixed seed blend.

Combine @flakey salt{50%g}, @black sesame seeds{50%g}, @white sesame seeds{50%g}, @poppy seeds{50%g}, @dehydrated minced garlic{50%g} and @dehydrated minced onion{50%g} in a #bowl{} and mix well.

-- ===== WHIPPED CREAM CHEESE SHMEAR =====

In a #stand mixer{}, whip @cream cheese{450%g}, @milk{3%tbsp} and @salt{1%pinch} for ~{2%minutes} until smooth and spreadable.